From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 88W8864: record a TX skb in the ring only after it is
 mapped

pcie_tx_skb() stored the skb in the TX handle before mapping it. When
the mapping failed, the skb was freed but the handle still pointed at
it. Record the skb only once it is mapped.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
[Robert Peerenboom: split out of neheb/mwlwifi (upstream branch) commit
 dcb73e4dca ("88W8864/88W8997: fix RX refill, TX status and teardown
 bugs") and backported to db97edf2 on top of the OpenWrt patches]
Signed-off-by: Robert Peerenboom <development@mindrush.de>
---
 hif/pcie/8864/tx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
@@ -266,7 +266,6 @@ static inline void pcie_tx_skb(struct mw
 	pcie_tx_add_dma_header(priv, tx_skb, 0, tailpad);
 
 	tx_hndl = pcie_priv->desc_data[desc_num].pnext_tx_hndl;
-	tx_hndl->psk_buff = tx_skb;
 	tx_desc = tx_hndl->pdesc;
 	dma_data = (struct pcie_dma_data *)tx_skb->data;
 	wh = &dma_data->wh;
@@ -293,6 +292,7 @@ static inline void pcie_tx_skb(struct mw
 		return;
 	}
 	tx_desc->pkt_ptr = cpu_to_le32(dma);
+	tx_hndl->psk_buff = tx_skb;
 	tx_desc->status = cpu_to_le32(EAGLE_TXD_STATUS_FW_OWNED);
 	/* make sure all the memory transactions done by cpu were completed */
 	wmb();	/*Data Memory Barrier*/
